			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Configure dev node environment and add extension scanning/user stub handlers\n\nConfigure Mountain for development node environment with verbose binary/library naming and add extension scanning improvements:\n\n1. **Dev Node Environment Setup**: Rename binary and library to `DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_Mountain` with corresponding tauri.conf.json changes including externalBin reference to `Binary/node`.\n\n2. **Extension Scanning Enhancements** (ScanPathConfigure.rs):\n   - Add VS Code-style bundle path: `.app/Contents/Resources/app/extensions`\n   - Add user-scope paths: `~/.codeeditorland/extensions` and `~/.land/extensions`\n   - Mirrors VS Code's `~/.vscode-oss/extensions` convention\n\n3. **Cocoon Health Monitor Fix** (CocoonManagement.rs):\n   - Stop flooding logs with \"No Cocoon process to monitor\" after crashes\n   - Monitor now exits quietly once process is gone instead of looping forever\n\n4. **Hover Provider Logging** (Provider.rs):\n   - Enhanced logging with handle, URI, position, and result details\n\n5. **IPC Stub Handlers** (CreateEffectForRequest.rs):\n   - Debug.Stop, Task.Fetch, Task.Execute\n   - Authentication.GetSession, Authentication.GetAccounts\n   - Clipboard.Read, Clipboard.Write, NativeHost.OpenExternal\n   - Languages.GetAll\n   These stubs return safe defaults (null/[]/\"\") to prevent extensions from crashing on unimplemented VS Code APIs.\n\nThese changes enable proper development workflow with user extension directories and prevent log flooding while providing foundation for future full implementations.",
			"SHA": "62187df95ab59673fc80a98c9e3bfdc8dc4342d2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-17T13:32:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				732,
				9
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct Sky path resolution and add extension scanning instrumentation\n\nThree related improvements to extension management and path resolution:\n\n1. **Fix Sky target path resolution** - The monorepo layout places Sky at `Land/Element/Sky/`, but the code was incorrectly using `Element/Sky/Target` (doubling Element). Change from `../../../Element/Sky/Target` to `../../../Sky/Target` in ScanPathConfigure.rs, AppLifecycle.rs, and InitializationData.rs.\n\n2. **Add dev-only cfg guards** - Wrap dev fallback paths in `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]` to keep release builds lean. Production should fail loudly if the bundle is misconfigured rather than silently falling back to dev paths.\n\n3. **Add extension scanning instrumentation** - Comprehensive logging throughout the scanning pipeline:\n   - ScanAndPopulateExtensions: track inserted vs rejected (empty identifier) counts\n   - Scanner: log directory entries, parse failures, missing package.json\n   - MountainEnvironment: verify serialized non-null extensions\n   - Extension handler: log serialized payload sizes, warn on empty results\n   - Also register native `setContext` command as no-op for VS Code extension compatibility\n\n4. **Implement FileSystem effects** - Add FileSystem.Stat, CreateDirectory, Delete, Rename, Copy effects to CreateEffectForRequest, completing the IPC bridge between Wind requests and Mountain's FileSystemReader/Writer traits.",
			"SHA": "3ba96f11406420784098879a309de9cd997c2fcf"
		},
